e(('c', 'f')));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next(), None);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Since the argument to `zip()` uses [`IntoIterator`], we can pass"},{"DocComment":" anything that can be converted into an [`Iterator`], not just an"},{"DocComment":" [`Iterator`] itself. For example, arrays (`[T]`) implement"},{"DocComment":" [`IntoIterator`], and so can be passed to `zip()` directly:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let a1 = [1, 2, 3];"},{"DocComment":" let a2 = [4, 5, 6];"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let mut iter = a1.into_iter().zip(a2);"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next(), Some((1, 4)));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next(), Some((2, 5)));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next(), Some((3, 6)));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next(), None);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" `zip()` is often used to zip an infinite iterator to a finite one."},{"DocComment":" This works because the finite iterator will eventually return [`None`],"},{"DocComment":" ending the zipper. Zipping with `(0..)` can look a lot like [`enumerate`]:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let enumerate: Vec<_> = \"foo\".chars().enumerate().collect();"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let zipper: Vec<_> = (0..).zip(\"foo\".chars()).collect();"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!((0, 'f'), enumerate[0]);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!((0, 'f'), zipper[0]);"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!((1, 'o'), enumerate[1]);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!((1, 'o'), zipper[1]);"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!((2, 'o'), enumerate[2]);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!((2, 'o'), zipper[2]);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" If both iterators have roughly equivalent syntax, it may be more readable to use [`zip`]:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" use std::iter::zip;"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let a = [1, 2, 3];"},{"DocComment":" let b = [2, 3, 4];"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let mut zipped = zip("},{"DocComment":"     a.into_iter().map(|x| x * 2).skip(1),"},{"DocComment":"     b.into_iter().map(|x| x * 2).skip(1),"},{"DocComment":" );"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(zipped.next(), Some((4, 6)));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(zipped.next(), Some((6, 8)));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(zipped.next(), None);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" compared to:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" # let a = [1, 2, 3];"},{"DocComment":" # let b = [2, 3, 4];"},{"DocComment":" #"},{"DocComment":" let mut zipped = a"},{"DocComment":"     .into_iter()"},{"DocComment":"     .map(|x| x * 2)"},{"DocComment":"     .skip(1)"},{"DocComment":"     .zip(b.into_iter().map(|x| x * 2).skip(1));"},{"DocComment":" #"},{"DocComment":" # assert_eq!(zipped.next(), Some((4, 6)));"},{"DocComment":" # assert_eq!(zipped.next(), Some((6, 8)));"},{"DocComment":" # assert_eq!(zipped.next(), None);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [`enumerate`]: Iterator::enumerate"},{"DocComment":" [`next`]: Iterator::next"},{"DocComment":" [`zip`]: crate::iter::zip"}],"inline":"Hint","rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"started_from":false,"is_extern":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null,"diagnostic_item":null,"has_errors":false},"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"Self","variance":"Unknown"},{"index":1,"name":"U","variance":"Invariant"},{"index":2,"name":"Clause0_Item","variance":"Invariant"},{"index":3,"name":"Clause1_Item","variance":"Invariant"},{"index":4,"name":"Clause1_IntoIter","variance":"Invariant"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[{"clause_id":0,"span":{"Deduplicated":391},"origin":"TraitSelf","trait_":{"regions":[],"outlives":[],"skip_binder":{"id":19,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Deduplicated":16},{"Deduplicated":43}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}},{"clause_id":1,"span":{"Value":[2086,{"data":{"file_id":35,"beg":{"line":646,"col":11},"end":{"line":646,"col":23}},"generated_from_span":null}]},"origin":"WhereClauseOnFn","trait_":{"regions":[],"outlives":[],"skip_binder":{"id":23,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Deduplicated":28},{"Value":[1124,{"TypeVar":{"Free":3}}]},{"Value":[1125,{"TypeVar":{"Free":4}}]}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}],"outlives":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"signature":{"is_unsafe":false,"abi":"Rust","is_variadic":false,"inputs":[{"Deduplicated":16},{"Deduplicated":28}],"output":{"Value":[1126,{"Adt":{"id":34,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Deduplicated":16},{"Deduplicated":1125}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":null}}]}},"src":{"TraitDefault":{"trait_ref":{"id":19,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Deduplicated":16},{"Deduplicated":43}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}},"item_id":9}},"body":"Opaque"},{"def_id":89,"item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["slice",0]},{"Impl":{"Ty":{"params":{"regions":[],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"T","variance":"Unknown"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"outlives":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"skip_binder":{"Deduplicated":7},"kind":"InherentImplBlock"}}},{"Ident":["chunks_exact",0]}],"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":3,"beg":{"line":1243,"col":4},"end":{"line":1243,"col":77}},"generated_from_span":null}},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Returns an iterator over `chunk_size` elements of the slice at a time, starting at the"},{"DocComment":" beginning of the slice."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The chunks are slices and do not overlap. If `chunk_size` does not divide the length of the"},{"DocComment":" slice, then the last up to `chunk_size-1` elements will be omitted and can be retrieved"},{"DocComment":" from the `remainder` function of the iterator."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Due to each chunk having exactly `chunk_size` elements, the compiler can often optimize the"},{"DocComment":" resulting code better than in the case of [`chunks`]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" See [`chunks`] for a variant of this iterator that also returns the remainder as a smaller"},{"DocComment":" chunk, and [`rchunks_exact`] for the same iterator but starting at the end of the slice."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" If your `chunk_size` is a constant, consider using [`as_chunks`] instead, which will"},{"DocComment":" give references to arrays of exactly that length, rather than slices."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Panics"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Panics if `chunk_size` is zero."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let slice = ['l', 'o', 'r', 'e', 'm'];"},{"DocComment":" let mut iter = slice.chunks_exact(2);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next().unwrap(), &['l', 'o']);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next().unwrap(), &['r', 'e']);"},{"DocComment":" assert!(iter.next().is_none());"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.remainder(), &['m']);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [`chunks`]: slice::chunks"},{"DocComment":" [`rchunks_exact`]: slice::rchunks_exact"},{"DocComment":" [`as_chunks`]: slice::as_chunks"},{"Builtin":{"TrackCaller":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":3,"beg":{"line":1242,"col":4},"end":{"line":1242,"col":19}},"generated_from_span":null}}}}],"inline":"Hint","rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"started_from":false,"is_extern":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null,"diagnostic_item":null,"has_errors":false},"generics":{"regions":[{"index":0,"name":null,"variance":"Invariant","mutability":"Unknown","late_bound":true}],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"T","variance":"Unknown"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"outlives":[{"regions":[],"outlives":[],"skip_binder":[{"Lub":{"Deduplicated":16}},{"Var":{"Free":0}}]}],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"signature":{"is_unsafe":false,"abi":"Rust","is_v